Saved `ADR-001-notification-architecture.md` with a definitive recommendation for **Redis Streams**.

The ADR recommends Redis Streams over Apache Kafka based on the team's operational constraints (6 engineers, no infra specialist, 2-week delivery window) and the workload profile (peak 500 req/s, 10× target ~5,000 req/s, ephemeral messages). It justifies the choice using specific technical properties—throughput headroom, per-stream ordering, memory-bound retention with `MAXLEN`, native consumer groups (`XREADGROUP`/`XCLAIM`), and application-level exactly-once via PostgreSQL idempotency keys—while explicitly rejecting Kafka due to operational complexity and lack of team experience at this scale.
